{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966805,"nonce":"rT/9O7KLIZnDJb4FS10AQYhk87Q=","title":"render_layer_range_tight skipped mesh aux_data offset","message":"`render_layer_range_tight` (blinc_gpu/renderer.rs) walks the\nprimitive range of an effect layer, subtracts\n`(layer_pos - effect_expansion)` from each `prim.bounds.xy`,\nand renders into a tight texture sized to the bbox. That\ntranslation is correct for SDF prim types 0-2 (rect / circle /\nellipse) — those read `prim.bounds.xy` as the geometry origin.\nMesh primitives (`type_info[0] == 9`) don't: the SDF vertex\nshader reads triangle vertex positions out of\n`aux_data[aux_offset]` and `aux_data[aux_offset + 1]`. Those\nare stored at push time in absolute screen coordinates by\n`push_mesh_primitives_brush`. The tight pass clamped them to\nthe texture viewport via the same `viewport_size`-based\nclip-space conversion every other primitive uses, so triangle\nvertices at e.g. `(220, 220)` rendered into a 192×128 tight\ntexture all landed outside `[-1, 1]` clip space — rasteriser\nclipped the triangle, the texture stayed empty, and the\npost-blur composite blitted a transparent square.\n\nFix in `d132cf8a`: clone `batch.aux_data`, walk\n`offset_primitives` for mesh entries, subtract the same\n`(offset_x, offset_y)` from each position vec4 (pack0.xyzw and\npack1.xy — pack1.zw is padding, per-vertex colour entries that\nfollow stay untouched), upload to the shared aux buffer for\nthe tight render, then write `batch.aux_data` back after\n`queue.submit` so subsequent passes (next layer's tight\nrender, dynamic images, path overlay) see screen-space\npositions again. DT fallback (`!has_storage_buffers`) routes\nthrough `update_aux_data_texture` symmetrically.\n\n**Why:** Symptom was reported on ruffle's `m1_keyframed_rotation`\ndemo — once the noop-effect filter was removed upstream so\nevery authored blur pushes a layer (consistent dispatch across\nthe breathe-blur cycle), the rect went through the layer-effect\npath on every frame. That tipped the mesh-aux gap, which had\nbeen masked while the rect rendered directly on no-op frames.\n\n**How to apply:** Anything that walks a primitive sub-range and\ntranslates positions for an offscreen pass needs to also walk\nthe aux buffer when mesh primitives are involved — `bounds.xy`\nis *not* the source of truth for mesh vertex positions. Same\ncaveat applies to any future tight-pass variant (3D effect\npasses, glass ranges, etc.). Per-vertex colour entries\n(`type_info[3] == 1` adds 3 vec4 of RGBA after the position\npair) stay untouched — the offset only applies to xyzw of the\nfirst two vec4s.","files":null}]}